  "knowledge": {
    "progressSummary": "SOLVED. New verified file CayleyHamiltonMinpolyOQ01OQ01OQ02.lean (16 theorems, 4 defs, 0 sorries, 0 axioms) recovers the Jordan block counts per size from the generalized-eigenspace dimension tower d_k(mu)=dim ker((f-mu)^k), with NO explicit Jordan basis (which Mathlib 4.26.0 lacks). The mathematical heart is the concavity of the tower d_{k+2}+d_k <= 2 d_{k+1}, proved via the antitone chain of image submodules N^k(ker N^{k+1}) whose dimensions are the successive differences d_{k+1}-d_k. blocksAtLeast (Weyr characteristic) and blocksExact are read off the tower with telescoping to the algebraic multiplicity, total count = geometric multiplicity, and #{size=k+1}=2 d_{k+1}-d_k-d_{k+2}. Eigenvalue interface bridges to Module.End.genEigenspace via genEigenspace_nat. #print axioms lists only propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound. PR #34409. Answers the parent entry oq-01-oq-01 stated open question.",
    "builtItems": [
      "nullity_succ: rank-nullity across one level, d_{k+1} = dim(N^k(ker N^{k+1})) + d_k, from finrank_range_add_finrank_ker on (N^k).domRestrict (ker N^{k+1})",
      "nullity_concave: concavity d_{k+2}+d_k <= 2 d_{k+1} (the crux), from jordanImage_antitone + finrank_mono + omega",
      "jordanImage_antitone: N maps N^{k+1}(ker N^{k+2}) into N^k(ker N^{k+1}) — the antitone image-submodule chain",
      "blocksAtLeast/blocksExact with sum_blocksAtLeast (telescopes to d_m), blocksAtLeast_one (total=geometric multiplicity), blocksExact_succ_tower (#{size=k+1}=2 d_{k+1}-d_k-d_{k+2})",
      "Eigenvalue interface: nullity_sub_eq_finrank_genEigenspace, eigenvalue_blocksAtLeast, eigenvalue_blocks_total, genEigenspace_finrank_concave"
    ],
    "insights": [
      "The Jordan block counts per size need no Jordan basis — the increasing kernel tower ker(N^k) and rank-nullity suffice, mirroring how the parent recovered the largest block size spectrally",
      "Blocks of size >= k+1 = dim(N^k(ker N^{k+1})), a concrete image submodule = tower difference d_{k+1}-d_k; concavity is the single antitone inclusion N.P_{k+1} subseteq P_k",
      "genEigenspace_nat is the one bridge lemma turning the abstract nullity tower of f-mu into dim(genEigenspace f mu k), transporting concavity and all block-count formulas to every eigenvalue",
      "set W caused omega atom-mismatch (W vs ker(N^{k+1})); keep explicit terms. pow_succ rewrites leftmost occurrence — use reversed mul_apply/pow_succ. simp only did not fire pow_zero/pow_one — use explicit rw with show"
    ],
